Review of spec:pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes at 2052d734a6fd.

Findings:

- N1, medium blocker: the Windows termination helpers are no-ops, so reviewer descendants can survive cleanup despite R1: [review_dispatch_windows.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-643624343/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch_windows.go:16). L2 documents this limit, but R1 has no platform exception.
- N2, low follow-up: the unshimmed fallback trusts a reviewer-controlled environment marker when selecting PIDs: [review_reap_linux.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-643624343/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go:102). The shipped Linux CLI uses the shim.
- N3, low follow-up: the shim materializes all of /proc before checking its deadline: [review_shim_linux.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-643624343/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go:134).

Focused regression tests, the expanded release/shim tests, the race-enabled concurrency subset, and go vet passed. Required strict validation was attempted; the matrix could not start checks because the read-only sandbox rejected Go build and cache writes. The completion gates are deferred because the task prohibits an attestation.

